# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS
# Two sources require this section:
#   - Game rulebook rules 39-40 (docs/RULES.md): never push secrets or
#     credentials, even to a private repo shared only with the lecturer.
#     Sanction: severe security failure and project failure.
#   - Engineering standard §7.4 (docs/SEGAL_GUIDELINES.md): .gitignore MUST
#     include .env, *.key, *.pem, credentials.json. Checked by automatic scan.
# These entries exist BEFORE the OAuth code does. Do not remove them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
credentials.json
*.key
*.pem

# .env-example carries dummy values and MUST be committed (§7.4)
!.env-example

client_secret*.json
token.json
token.pickle
*.token
secrets/
.secrets/
*_secret*
*-secret*

# These test files legitimately have "secret" in the NAME (they test the
# D-56 shared-secret guard) but hold no real secret value -- only
# placeholder literals local to the test. Explicit negations, same
# precedent as .env-example above.
!tests/unit/test_secret_guard.py
!tests/unit/test_secret_wiring.py
!tests/unit/test_peer_runtime_secret.py
!tests/integration/test_secret_channel.py

# Nonces must stay secret until end of game (rule 18) — never commit live ones
nonces/
*.nonce

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# Testing / coverage
#
# The XML pair is 08-03's §17 "automated test reports" deliverable, produced by
# the CI job and uploaded as a run artifact. They are BUILD OUTPUT — regenerable
# with the one command written into .github/workflows/quality-gate.yml — so they
# are ignored here for the same reason graph.json is: a per-run file committed by
# reflex produces diffs nobody reads and evidence nobody can date.
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
# Anchored: both are written at the workspace root by the command above, and an
# unanchored `reports/` would silently swallow a `docs/reports/` somebody adds.
/coverage.xml
/reports/
htmlcov/
.tox/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project runtime artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trained Q-tables can be large; commit deliberately, not by accident
*.qtable
models/checkpoints/

# Rule 37/38's per-role games-played counter is mutable runtime state, not
# fixed config -- persisted BESIDE config/{police,thief}/ by design (06-03)
# so it survives across real games, but never version-controlled, same
# reasoning as *.qtable/nonces/ above. Its *.prev durable-write rotation
# generation is covered by the same glob.
config/*/games_played*.json

# Local run output: per-run wire logs (<uid>.jsonl) and nonce ledgers
# (<uid>.ledger.jsonl). Bulky, regenerable, deliberately not version-
# controlled — same reasoning as *.qtable above.
#
# D7-1 (07-02), correcting this comment. It used to read "the four required
# JSON artifacts (declaration_/config_/log_/result_) MUST be committed per
# rule 50 and Appendix F rule 4 — keep them out of this ignore list", while
# the very next line ignored logs/ wholesale and
# agent_step0_wiring.write_declaration wrote declaration_<game_id>.json into
# logs/<role>/. The comment was false and that is what let the contradiction
# survive: a document certifying a wrong fact turns every reader away at the
# door. The rule below is CORRECT and stays byte-unchanged.
#
# The four deliverable artifacts go to game_artifacts/ instead — the
# artifact_dir config/*/reporting.json sets, verified not ignored — and
# services/reporting/artifacts.write_artifact REFUSES any path under logs/,
# so the spine cannot regress back into this tree. Narrowing this rule was
# the rejected alternative: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so it would take a logs/** + negation restructure
# that the next editor can silently break, and it would put the bulky
# per-run output one careless `git add` away from the repository.
logs/
*.log
runs/
tmp/

# D7-19 (07-09). `game_artifacts/` is deliberately NOT ignored -- that is D7-1's
# whole resolution, because rule 50 and Appendix F rule 4 require the four JSON
# artifacts to be COMMITTABLE. The cost is that every scripts/dev_launch.py run
# leaves untracked files there, and one `git add -A` would publish a throwaway
# local game under filenames a grader reads as league evidence.
#
# Only the two patterns that can NEVER be one of those four artifacts are
# ignored here, and nothing else:
#   *.eml        the rendered RFC 5322 message a DRY RUN writes beside the
#                report. Not JSON, not one of the four names, never required.
#   *.prev.json  durable_write_json's rotation generation. `.prev` is not a
#                name docs/PARAMETERS.md:165-168 gives.
# The four required names (declaration_/config_/log_/result_) stay tracked and
# tracked-able, and tests/unit/test_artifact_dir_hygiene.py asserts BOTH halves
# -- that these two are ignored and that the four are not -- so narrowing this
# further would fail there rather than quietly hide league evidence.
game_artifacts/**/*.eml
game_artifacts/**/*.prev.json

# Tunnel config may embed auth tokens
ngrok.yml
ngrok.yaml
.localtonet/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source specification PDFs — copyrighted course material
# Rule 49 requires both submission repos to be PUBLIC. These PDFs are
# (c) Dr. Yoram Segal and are not ours to redistribute. They stay on disk as
# the local source of truth; the translated extracts in docs/ are committed
# instead. Remove these two lines only if the lecturer authorises publishing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
police_thief_p2p.pdf
software_submission_guidelines-V3.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Knowledge graph (graphify)
# graph.json and graph.html are ~2 MB each and are regenerable at zero API cost
# with `graphify update .`. Committing them would multiply the size of .git on
# every refresh and produce diffs no human can read. Only GRAPH_REPORT.md
# (~68 KB markdown) is committed, so a fresh clone — and the grader — still gets
# the navigable map. See CLAUDE.md "Knowledge graph (graphify)".
#
# THE ROOT-LEVEL PAIR WAS NOT COVERED UNTIL 08-03. `graphify update .` writes
# `graphify-out/` AND drops `graph.json` / `graph.html` at the repository root;
# only the `graphify-out/` and `.planning/graphs/` copies were ignored, so
# `git check-ignore -q graph.json` exited 1 while CLAUDE.md stated in as many
# words that both are gitignored build artifacts. The rules below are anchored
# with a leading slash so they cover exactly those two root artifacts and cannot
# hide a `graph.json` that some future subdirectory legitimately tracks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
graphify-out/
/graph.json
/graph.html
.planning/graphs/graph.json
.planning/graphs/graph.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent harness config
# .claude/settings.json IS committed — it carries the SessionStart graph hook
# that every agent depends on. Everything else under .claude/ is per-machine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
.codex/

